      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1893-07-01_WidnesExaminer_art0112" n="art0112">
        <head>ROYAL MARRIAGE cELEaltAzitms</head>
        <p>ROYAL MARRIAGE cELEaltAzitms</p>
        <p>•FOR WIDNES.</p>
        <p>Last week mad there appeared cousideaakle doubt whether the• amount necessary for chivying out these celebraCions oat Thursday nexn would be forthcoming,-, but a collecting cotr&lt;harttee was appointed hitt their aorta have been crEkwried with considerable.. suceeee, On Friday nit last the subscriptiorm•Sotalleti £l2O 14s Gd : ate meeting of the committee on Thursday night Mr. Councillor F. Neil; the, chai rinan,. announced that 22 rag 61 had now beer re:mired, a fact that was. greeted with applause. 'Mare WWI a large attendanee of delegates who proecs,ied• to moat) arrangements fatrthedemonstra- tion. Frtora.: returns submitted by the Town Clerk it appeared that then! were few short of 7.X1.000 children in the varioua.Sundar and day scbools„and to prtvide a tea and some little amusement for thsse it was calcu-</p>
        <p>lated titst sixpence per head wouldltost £250. It huh! been previously decided that o nanagers o. each Sunday school should wange for its owes holars; an it was now resolve, that they be piiii a grant, of sixpence per head to cover tea, It transpired that there were I,l3sdeildren who attoxiind the drip shoos, but not Sunday Schools, and the dill- ctittyt-of providing for theae prow:sod consideralle.dis• cussion. Reentuallv it was unanimously agresatthat those should apply for tickets 4.4 the Town Hall eniWed-, nesday and that the Town Mek allocate thesulto the !Stinestv Schools in such proporkions as were found con- xeuient and that they he pad ir.r pro raja. At was fur- ther resolved not to provide, commemoration&amp; usiedals of the children, but to make every effort to give&amp; treat to the aged poor. A united prooession of the children wiq be held, bu', the order in which the schools shall pro- CNN] has not yet been fixed ly the Procession Com- mittee. The place o scra"-ly is the. Town Hall &amp;rare. And the time one o'clock.</p>
        <p>A receiving order was made on Wednesday, in thl ,rulon Bankruptcy Court, against Mr. Peter M‘Lagann •,x-AI.P., tor Litilitligowshire.</p>
        <p>Tvre.fresh cases of cholera are reported from Toaltl, and one ck:e from Byeres,ami one from La Seyne,</p>
