        <p>QUARTERLY_ MEETING.</p>
        <p>_ . At a recent meeting the Rev. Wi.llinni Arrawemith movud, and Mr.kil Nuiveton seconded, a memorial to the WeSlevairetnifereisce about .to sit' in Cardiff, as follows r----Thia quarterly meeting of the Runcorn Circuit being paint ully impreseed with the alarming increase of the evil oS gambling, respectfully memorializes the Conference•tn pass a resolutien, as a means of lessening the temptations to and facilities for gambling, requesting the preen of Great Britain to ex- clude from its columns to the utmost possible extent all statements of' betting trannelions. This was carried unanitnousily. • During the meeting the Rev. A. Burnet, from BangalorcOndia, delivered an address on mission- ary work in Ihdia•witil special reference to current con- troversial matters. The rev-. gentleman invited ques- tions, whirligig-every tIASP wero satisfactorily answered. As a result the following reschatiora Was unanimously adopted i—nesolved, that this meeting having had the pleasure of a, lengthy conversation with the Rev. A. Burnet, of Bangalore,,ou the•ceserent Indian controversy, desires to place on record its admiration and apprecia- tion of his courteous; frank,. and satisfactory explana- tions of all the questions sunteitted to him, and ex- presses its confidence in the character and work of our Indian missionaries; and that a; copy of this resolution be sent to the Methodist papers.</p>
