        <p>Secretaries of Cricket Clubs are requested to note that teports of matches played on Saturday must be sent to the tread office, Bewsev-street. Warrington. not later than ten o'clock on Wednesday morning. ---- CRICKETERS. Lawn Tennisers, and Golfers are reminded that GEO. G. HUSSEY &amp; Co., rsThufacture high-class , requisites. Their new catalogue is obtainable from Local Dealers. or the Scots ManufacMry, Peckham Eye, S.E. I Trade 4.CCOh Mark. I ORFORD CRESCENT V. STOCKTON BEATll.—Plaved on Saturday. The result was an easy victory for Orford. Score :—Orford Crescent, 83 ; Stockton Heath, 36. SANKEY VIRE MILLS JUNIORS V. WYCLIFFE JUNIORS.— This match was played on the ground of the former, on Saturday, and resulted in a win for Sankey by seven runs. Score :—Sankey, 21 ; Wycliffe. 14. RUNCORN WHITE ROSE V. WIDNES RED ROSE.—Played at Widnes on Saturday, and ended in a win for the visitors by 25 runs.—Score White Rose, 62 ; Red Rose, 37. WESTON V. ROYAL MAIL SS. MAJ-ESTIC.,—The officers and crew of the SS. Majestic paid .a visit to Weston to play the village team, and after a pleasant game the homesters were victorious. For the visitors Mr. Aitchi- son played a splendid game for his 17 not out, and Mr. Dawson took four wickets for 14 runs, whilst for the home team Mr. Tudor, sen.. played well for 28, and Mr. Tudor, jun., took six wickets for 18 runs. Score:— Weston, 62 ; SS. Majestic. 43: BUCKLE.Y ST. V. ST. PETER'S.—ThiS match was played on Saturday on the ground of the latter, and resulted in a win for the visitors. Score.:— DUCKLKY-STREET. ST. PETER'S. Mass,-y c and is Morris ... 6 Morris is Hinchilffe 1 Marsh c Wildman b Gar ry c Leech b Pugh 4 Morris J Puirti c and b Garry ...... 8 Whittaker c Hinchliffe b A Pugh lbw Hinchliff c Sumner b H Sumner b Hinchliffe Morris Haddock c Lawton b Jolley not out 8 Mcrrris Turner c Morris h Garry 1 life 4 As Leech not out J Leech is Garry Cook b Garry 4 Webster is Hinchliffe. Crank c Jolley is Morris 1 Extras 5 Extra