        <p>ISILVER MEDAL, EDINBURGH, 1890 GOLD MEDAL JAMAICA, 1891. GOLD MEDAL, DERBY, 1891. COLEMAN'S WINCARNIS, ' OR LIEBIG'S EXTRACT OF MEAT AND MALT WINE. WINCARNIS Is the New Name Rettis'ered to Prevent Fraudulent Imitations. OVER TWO THOUSAND Unsolicited Testimonials have been received from Medical Men. IMPORTANT UNSOLICITED TESTIMONIAL FROM Dr. MATTHEWS. Derehatn-road. Norwich. Dereham-road, Norwich, June 13th. 1891 Gentlemen,—You have been kind enou.th to send me several tree orders for your " Wincarnis." and it has given much r.- lief to several who were in a dying state—they could take the " Wincarnis "when everything else was rejected, I am now begging the favour of asking you if you can do a w;,rk of charity in giving a podr dying man some of your ' Wincarnis." It Arts kept him up some weeks. He is suffer- ing from an internal cancer. Ills means are all gone. Friends and his family have purchased two large battles weekly— They cannot afford him more. Ile has had the most expen- sive wines, but nothing suits him Ilk,- the" Wincarnis." The case is urgent. 'lli • gentleman has tilled an important posi- tion in this county,but his meansare gone.—Yours faithfully, W. MATTHEWS. Messrs. Coleman and Co., Limited. WLNCARNIS Is sold by all Druggists, Wine Merchants, and Patent Medici, e Vendors. Ask for COLEMAN'S "WI NCALINIS," or LIEBIG'S EXTRACT OF MEAT AND MALT WINE, and see that the word WINCARNIS is on the shoulder of the bottle. If there is any difficulty in getting the Wine, write direct to the Manufacturers, who will forward Sample Pint Bottle Free by Post on receipt of 33 stamps. „ Doz. „ Rail PI 30s. Sole Manufacturer!: COLEMAN &amp; CO., Limd, .':t. George's and Bank Plain, Norwich ; end 3, New London-st., London, W.C. Sole Proprietors of " Ozin,zon," the New Beef Tea, and also Coleman's Crown Imperial Invalid Stout, which is strongly recommended by the Medical Faculty.</p>
